.env
# direnv. A fact about one machine — on NixOS it puts nix-ld's libstdc++ on
# LD_LIBRARY_PATH so greenlet's compiled extension loads. See CLAUDE.md.
.envrc
.direnv/
# config/config.yaml *is* tracked — it holds the demo defaults, and a fresh
# clone has to be able to run. This is the local overlay deep-merged over it,
# which is where a machine-specific model endpoint goes. Same bargain .env makes.
config/config.local.yaml
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.claude/
.omc/

# demo/demo.gif is committed — the README embeds it. The mp4 is a by-product of
# the same take and would double the repo's weight for nothing.
demo/*.mp4
# The harvested prompt corpus. Gitignored not for tidiness: a case holds the
# recorded prompt, and a trace holds whatever the registered warehouse holds,
# so committing a harvest commits customer data by construction. The *authored*
# probes in tests/probes/ are the opposite — those are contract, like
# tests/test_traps.py.
optim/out/
